<speak>That sounds like a fairly big adjustment in your daily routine, even if the business itself is familiar territory. When responsibilities move around within a family, the informal arrangements sometimes take longer to change than the job titles. People still knock on the door they have always knocked on. For the administrative side of our relationship, we can keep our contact with you predictable rather than adding another interruption. You can tell me which parts of the day tend to be quieter, and we can use those for ordinary calls. There is no need for you to be available whenever the office happens to be busy.</speak>